      },
      "inLanguage": "en-GB",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/land-rover-2.2#faq-question-1",
          "name": "Is the Land Rover 2.2 diesel engine reliable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can be reliable with consistent servicing, but turbo wear and HP fuel pump failure are well-documented issues as these engines age. Reliability depends heavily on service history, mileage and how quickly early symptoms like reduced power were investigated."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/land-rover-2.2#faq-question-2",
          "name": "What are the common faults with the Freelander 2 engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Turbo failure and high-pressure fuel pump failure are the two most frequently reported issues on the Freelander 2's 2.2 diesel. Both can produce similar symptoms, including power loss, so proper diagnosis is needed to identify which component is actually at fault."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/land-rover-2.2#faq-question-3",
          "name": "Can a failed HP fuel pump damage other engine parts?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, when the high-pressure fuel pump fails, it can release metal debris into the fuel system, contaminating injectors and the fuel rail. This is why a full fuel system flush is often necessary alongside pump replacement, rather than fitting a new pump alone."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/land-rover-2.2#faq-question-4",
          "name": "What's the difference between the TD4 and SD4 engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Both use the same 2.2 litre 224DT engine block, but the SD4 is tuned for higher power output than the TD4. The core turbo and fuel pump fault patterns are broadly similar across both tunes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/land-rover-2.2#faq-question-5",
          "name": "Which Land Rover models use the 2.2 diesel engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The 2.2 TD4 and SD4 were fitted to the Freelander 2, Discovery 4 and early Discovery Sport models before later generations moved to Ingenium engines. Confirming the exact vehicle and engine code helps with accurate diagnosis and parts sourcing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/land-rover-2.2#faq-question-6",
          "name": "How much does a Land Rover 2.2 engine replacement cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Cost depends on whether a turbo repair, fuel pump replacement, rebuild or full engine replacement is appropriate, along with the extent of any contamination or damage found. We assess each vehicle individually and provide a clear, itemised quote once diagnosis is complete."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/land-rover-2.2#faq-question-7",
          "name": "Do reconditioned 2.2 diesel engines come with a warranty?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, reconditioned and replacement engines are supplied with warranty cover. We'll confirm the specific terms for your engine before any work is booked, so you know exactly what's included."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/land-rover-2.2#faq-question-8",
          "name": "What areas do you cover for Land Rover engine work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We're based in Grays, Essex, and regularly support customers across Essex, London and the wider South East, alongside UK-wide enquiries for engine supply and fitting. Get in touch to confirm availability for your location."
          }
        }
      ]
